{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>Let no man go out</b> Three times in the Masorah: here, and another: <b>אל יצא פליט מן העיר</b> (let no fugitive go out from the city) — <b>בואו הכום איש אל יצא</b> (let no man go out from his place). <b>אל יצא איש ממקומו</b> — this is beyond four cubits, because he went beyond the boundary: <b>אל יצא פליט מן העיר</b> — this is the Shabbat boundary. <b>בואו הכום איש אל יצא</b> — hint to בית דין (Beit Din): lashes for eruvin of boundaries, Torah law."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The text reads 'הע. ר' with a space/dot in 'העיר'; translated as the single word העיר (the city) per the biblical verse (Joshua 8:22). The third occurrence is from 2 Samuel 18:17."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:16.514528219Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}